const e="aliwan-fiesta-street-dance-philippines",h=2026,t="Read in full: the Activities page and the six activity pages, the FAQs page (2026), the About pages, the home page, the Terms of Use and Privacy pages, and the published Updates (2023 and 2024 press posts), with every rule-bearing one read in full. The site publishes no rulebook, so every rule is taken from the organiser's own updates and is marked with the year it was printed. The rules for the 2026 edition are only 'Kindly wait for announcements' (venue, start time, entry deadline, registration, photo competition, voting end date) and the dates May 7 to 9, 2026. Captured from the 2023 and 2024 updates: eligibility for each competition, judging criteria, performance times for Tugtog ng Aliwan, prizes, special awards, the Reyna segments and rules, the photography terms, bazaar contacts, and the programme of 2024. Facts that the template maintenance note says were not asserted because no organiser document states them (a fixed 17 regions x 2 contingents structure, LGU pre-registration for contingents, contingent size caps) are still not stated. Only the organiser's printed lines are used: 'only two entries per province' (2023) and 'LGUs may field entries' for Reyna (2023). Not printed, so left empty: any entry fee, contingent size, the performance time for the Streetdance in 2026, the Float rules beyond the criteria, an age limit above 16 for Reyna, and any points for placings. The About and Updates pages also print winner lists, candidate lists and artist lines; they are results and publicity, not rules, and are not written here except the award names. Template note: the group age bands (Contingents 12-99, Reyna 16-30) are the template's own; the site prints only 'aged 16 and above' for Reyna.",a={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"Aliwan Fiesta, the Philippines' Grand Festival of Champions. Rules, criteria and prizes printed by the organiser.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"Aliwan Fiesta 2026 is on {{EventStartDate}} to {{EventEndDate}}. The venue, start times and entry deadline are not announced yet: kindly wait for announcements. Where a fact below comes from the 2023 or 2024 edition, the sentence says so.",Notes:["How to register: {{HowToRegister}}","Entry deadline: {{EntryDeadline}}","Aliwan Fiesta is free to watch. There is no registration for the three-night event.","Photography competition: {{PhotoDeadline}}"],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General Rules",Items:["Aliwan Fiesta is the Philippines' Grand Festival of Champions. It has run since 2003. The organiser is Manila Broadcasting Company (MBC), also called MBC Media Group. In 2024 it was organised in partnership with the City of Pasay, the City of Manila and the Cultural Center of the Philippines.","It is a three-day event. The main events are the Pasakalye concert, the Shoppers' Bazaar, the Reyna ng Aliwan pageant, the Float Parade and Streetdance Competition, and the Awarding Ceremony. The Tugtog ng Aliwan festival music competition and the Photography Competition are also held.","There are five official competitions: the Streetdance Competition, the Float Parade Competition, Reyna ng Aliwan, Tugtog ng Aliwan and the Aliwan Fiesta Photography Competition. A Netizens' Choice public vote runs with Reyna ng Aliwan.","The organisers and the judging panel stress both artistic excellence and following local culture and practices. Participants are urged to use authentic cultural elements specific to their localities.","Aliwan Fiesta is free. There are no tickets. There is no registration to watch the three-night event.","There is no application for a media pass for content creators. Aliwan Fiesta is open for everyone. There is a designated place for photographers on the 3rd day, first come, first served.","In 2023, three days of events were open to everyone, with bleachers set aside for the audience.","For first aid, rescue and emergency tents and for parking areas, the FAQs say to check the official pages (the links are not in the page text). Traffic advisories on road closures and alternative routes will be published soon."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Who Can Take Part",Items:["Streetdance: the contingents are hand-picked to represent their region's festival through local competitions. They come from Luzon, Visayas and Mindanao (2023 announcement).","Streetdance: the competition is open not only to distinguished festivals but also to obscure but consequential feasts all over Luzon, Visayas and Mindanao (2023 announcement).","Streetdance: only two entries per province are allowed (2023 announcement).","Streetdance: movements must be enhanced by live music and fully show the local colour of the community (2023 announcement).","Float Parade: entries should creatively show the economic perspective of the town or province they represent (2023 announcement).","Tugtog ng Aliwan: open to all official musicians of the contingents taking part in the festival dance competition (2024 announcement).","Photography Competition: open to amateur and professional photographers (2024 announcement).","Reyna ng Aliwan: candidates are aged 16 and above and represent festivals of their hometowns (2024 announcement).","Reyna ng Aliwan: candidates must be naturally born women, according to the competition mechanics stated by the MBC Media Group president at the 2024 press conference. He hinted at possible future adjustments.","Reyna ng Aliwan: local government units (LGUs) may field entries (2023 announcement).","Reyna ng Aliwan: past Aliwan Fiesta Digital Queen candidates and winners could join Reyna ng Aliwan 2023 if they were endorsed as the festival queen of their locality (2023 announcement).","Netizens' Choice voting: you must register on the website to vote."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to Register",Items:["How can participants register on competitions? {{HowToRegister}}","Deadline for entries: {{EntryDeadline}}","For the 2023 festival, the registration notice for streetdance and float printed a deadline of June 16 and an email for enquiries: {{RegistrationEmail2023}}.","Regional Bazaar booths: to secure a slot or register, send your inquiries to {{BazaarContact}}.","Photography Competition: {{PhotoDeadline}}","Where to find information about events and schedule: the Aliwan Fiesta website and the official social media accounts. {{SocialMedia}}"]},{Key:"dates",Title:"Dates and Times",Items:["Aliwan Fiesta 2026 is set on {{EventStartDate}} to {{EventEndDate}}.","What time do events start? {{StartTime}}","For reference, the 2024 programme was: {{Schedule2024}}","In 2023 the festival was on July 13 to 15, with the Pasakalye concert on day 1, the Reyna ng Aliwan pageant on day 2, and the Grand Parade and Awarding Ceremonies on day 3. The 2023 date was set to follow the academic calendar."]},{Key:"venue",Title:"Venue",Items:["Where does Aliwan Fiesta 2026 take place? {{Venue}}","Live coverage: {{LiveCoverage}}"]},{Key:"fees",Title:"Fees",Items:["Aliwan Fiesta is free to watch. There are no ticket sales.","The organiser's pages print no entry fee for the competitions."]},{Key:"prizes",Title:"Prizes and Awards",Items:["Winners of the competitions are crowned and given rewards such as cash and trophies at the Awarding Ceremony.","Streetdance: {{StreetdanceGrandPrize}}","Float Parade: {{FloatGrandPrize}}","Reyna ng Aliwan: {{ReynaPrize}}","Tugtog ng Aliwan: {{TugtogPrizes}}","Photography Competition: {{PhotoPrizes}}","Winning photography entries become the property of MBC Media Group. The organiser can publish or exhibit the material for promotional purposes. The owner of the photo is still named when it is posted.","Netizens' Choice Awards: the public votes online and the candidate with the most votes wins the Netizens' Choice Award."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Judging",Items:["A panel of judges evaluates each contingent (2023 awarding report) and each candidate.","Each competition's marking criteria are given in that competition's rules.","For the Photography Competition the 2024 judges were Mr. George Tapan, Mr. Jophel Ybiosa and Mr. Jimmy Domingo. The 2023 judges were Romy Vitug, George Tapan and Wig Tysmans."]},{Key:"other",Title:"Shoppers' Bazaar and Other Activities",Items:["Shoppers' Bazaar: a three-day showcase of the best products from the regions of the Philippines. In 2023 the regional bazaar was tied to the One Town One Product campaign of the Department of Trade and Industry (DTI). The shops open after the opening ceremony and run during the main festivities.","Who can take a bazaar booth (2023 notice): boutiques selling island ready-to-wear, footwear, jewelry and accessories, handicraft shops, stores and restaurants selling gourmet delicacies, fruit and flower farms, weaving cooperatives, tribal showrooms, free-trade organisations and other NGOs marketing local produce.","Bazaar booth inquiries: {{BazaarContact}}. In 2023: {{BazaarEmail2023}}.","Pasakalye concert: a free live concert of popular artists at the start of Aliwan Fiesta (details of each year's artists are in the updates).","In 2024 a four-episode show 'Inside Aliwan Fiesta The Primer' (June 24, 25, 26 and July 1) looked at the festival: the Pasakalye Concert, the Reyna ng Aliwan candidates, the Grand Parade and a post-event show 'The Best of the Best'.","The website terms of use: users must be of legal age, give truthful information, keep their account password private, and may not post unlawful, obscene, hateful, defamatory or false material. The Terms of Use is the organiser's website agreement.","Social media and updates: {{SocialMedia}}"]}],Documents:[{Title:"Aliwan Fiesta Activities",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/activities"},{Title:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs (2026)",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/faqs"},{Title:"Streetdance & Float Competitions at Aliwan Fiesta 2023",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/updates/mI-fLxy6RUP/streetdance-float-competitions-at-aliwan-fiesta-2023"},{Title:"Aliwan Fiesta 2024 reveals dance parade, float competition participants (prizes and criteria)",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/updates/j_E__KbQEzR/aliwan-fiesta-2024-reveals-dance-parade-float-competition-participants"},{Title:"Amplifying Filipino music heritage: Tugtog ng Aliwan is back! (rules and criteria)",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/updates/0kwc55fi2sN/amplifying-filipino-music-heritage-tugtog-ng-aliwan-is-back"},{Title:"Aliwan Fiesta Photo Competition: Showcasing talents through photography",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/updates/jBKWkby18n4/aliwan-fiesta-photo-competition-showcasing-talents-through-photography"},{Title:"Festival Queen search reaches a fever pitch at Aliwan Fiesta 2024 (Reyna criteria)",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/updates/jKbO3hYEfu1/festival-queen-search-reaches-a-fever-pitch-at-aliwan-fiesta-2024"}]},n=[],i=[{AgeGroup:"Reyna ng Aliwan",Source:"Update 'Festival Queen search reaches a fever pitch at Aliwan Fiesta 2024' (19 Jun 2024); Update 'Aliwan Fiesta 2024 unveils festivities with a press conference and official presentation of Reyna ng Aliwan Candidates' (24 Jun 2024)",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Candidates are aged 16 and above. The pages print no upper age limit.","Candidates must be naturally born women according to the competition mechanics."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Candidates are aged 16 and above. The pages print no upper age limit.
- Candidates must be naturally born women according to the competition mechanics.`}],o=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Streetdance Competition","Source":"Aliwan Fiesta Activities pages (Streetdance Competition); Update 'Aliwan Fiesta 2024 reveals dance parade, float competition participants' (5 Jun 2024); Update 'Streetdance & Float Competitions at Aliwan Fiesta 2023' (9 Jun 2023); Update 'Celebrating unity and diversity through cultural street dance and grand float' (18 May 2023); Update 'Dinagyang Festival Secures Back-to-Back Win, Pasigarbo Festival Reigns as Reyna ng Aliwan 2024' (30 Jun 2024); Update 'Aliwan Fiesta 2023 wraps up the Grand Parade with the best of the best' (15 Jul 2023)","Sections":{"About":["Dancers in elaborate costumes pay homage to the country's diverse festivals, traditions and history. The heart of Aliwan Fiesta beats strongest here.","It is the only venue where winners of local street dance competitions from Luzon, Visayas and Mindanao compete with each other (2023 article)."],"TimeAndFormat":["The competition is held in the Grand Parade. In 2024 contingents performed six-minute routines in front of the Aliw Theater, after a 2-minute performance in front of the Cultural Center of the Philippines.","In 2023 the contingents' first performance was at Harbor Square, then in front of the CCP, then a final full performance in front of the Aliw Theater."],"Rules":["Use authentic cultural elements specific to the locality when making the entry.","Movements must be enhanced by live music and fully show the local colour of the community.","Only two entries per province are allowed (2023 announcement)."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Theme/concept: 35%. Choreography: 20%. Performance: 20%. Costume: 15%. Props: 10%. (Criteria printed in 2024.)"],"Points":["Awards in 2023 and 2024: grand champion, 2nd, 3rd, 4th and 5th placers, five runners-up, and special citations.","Special awards printed for 2024: Pride of Place, Best Costume, Best Musical Accompaniment. In 2023 the special citations were Best in Costume, Best in Music Accompaniment and Best in Folkloric Performance.","The grand prize and the special award money are in the Prizes section."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Dancers in elaborate costumes pay homage to the country's diverse festivals, traditions and history. The heart of Aliwan Fiesta beats strongest here.\\n- It is the only venue where winners of local street dance competitions from Luzon, Visayas and Mindanao compete with each other (2023 article).\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The competition is held in the Grand Parade. In 2024 contingents performed six-minute routines in front of the Aliw Theater, after a 2-minute performance in front of the Cultural Center of the Philippines.\\n- In 2023 the contingents' first performance was at Harbor Square, then in front of the CCP, then a final full performance in front of the Aliw Theater.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Use authentic cultural elements specific to the locality when making the entry.\\n- Movements must be enhanced by live music and fully show the local colour of the community.\\n- Only two entries per province are allowed (2023 announcement).\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Theme/concept: 35%. Choreography: 20%. Performance: 20%. Costume: 15%. Props: 10%. (Criteria printed in 2024.)\\n\\n## Points\\n- Awards in 2023 and 2024: grand champion, 2nd, 3rd, 4th and 5th placers, five runners-up, and special citations.\\n- Special awards printed for 2024: Pride of Place, Best Costume, Best Musical Accompaniment. In 2023 the special citations were Best in Costume, Best in Music Accompaniment and Best in Folkloric Performance.\\n- The grand prize and the special award money are in the Prizes section."},{"Title":"Float Parade Competition","Source":"Aliwan Fiesta Activities pages (Float Parade); Update 'Aliwan Fiesta 2024 reveals dance parade, float competition participants' (5 Jun 2024); Update 'Streetdance & Float Competitions at Aliwan Fiesta 2023' (9 Jun 2023); Update 'Dinagyang Festival Secures Back-to-Back Win, Pasigarbo Festival Reigns as Reyna ng Aliwan 2024' (30 Jun 2024); Update 'Aliwan Fiesta 2023 wraps up the Grand Parade with the best of the best' (15 Jul 2023)","Sections":{"About":["Meticulously crafted floats with vibrant colours show the country's festivals, traditions and history.","The floats are made with natural materials and embellishing elements and tell the historic stories of their places (2023 article)."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Float entries should creatively show the economic perspective of the town or province they represent (2023 announcement).","The float competition supports the festival dance showdown and runs in the Grand Parade."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Craftsmanship: 50%. Theme: 25%. Overall impact and ingenuity: 25%. (Criteria printed in 2024.)"],"Points":["Awards in 2024: Best in Float, 2nd place, 3rd runner-up and runners-up. Awards in 2023: Best in Float, first place, 2nd runner-up and seven runners-up."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Meticulously crafted floats with vibrant colours show the country's festivals, traditions and history.\\n- The floats are made with natural materials and embellishing elements and tell the historic stories of their places (2023 article).\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Float entries should creatively show the economic perspective of the town or province they represent (2023 announcement).\\n- The float competition supports the festival dance showdown and runs in the Grand Parade.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Craftsmanship: 50%. Theme: 25%. Overall impact and ingenuity: 25%. (Criteria printed in 2024.)\\n\\n## Points\\n- Awards in 2024: Best in Float, 2nd place, 3rd runner-up and runners-up. Awards in 2023: Best in Float, first place, 2nd runner-up and seven runners-up."},{"Title":"Tugtog ng Aliwan (Festival Music)","Source":"Update 'Amplifying Filipino music heritage: Tugtog ng Aliwan is back!' (14 Jun 2024); Update 'Aliwan Fiesta 2024 heats up with Tugtog ng Aliwan tilt' (11 Jun 2024); Update 'Aliwan Fiesta Highlights: Dinagyang Festival wins Tugtog ng Aliwan, Now Trending: The Pasakalye Concert hits high notes' (28 Jun 2024)","Sections":{"About":["The Festival Music Competition began in 2017. It is a sidelight of the Aliwan Fiesta competitions and highlights the musical talent of Filipinos from all over the country.","It is held on the first day of the festival. In 2024 it was on June 27 at 5 PM in front of the Aliw Theater."],"TimeAndFormat":["The presentation lasts at least four (4) minutes and at most five (5) minutes.","A penalty of one (1) point is taken from the total score of all judges for every 10 seconds below four (4) minutes or beyond five (5) minutes."],"Rules":["Each ensemble must present a medley of one song endemic to the area or region it represents, mashed with one verse and one stanza of the Aliwan theme song.","Open to all official musicians of the contingents that take part in the festival dance competition.","Groups must perform in full costume."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Movements that unduly endanger the safety of the musicians are prohibited.","No electronic instruments, pre-recorded instrumentation or vocals."],"Judging":["Musicality (arrangement, tonal quality, harmony): 50%. Showmanship (dynamics and technique, including costumes and choreography): 40%. Audience impact: 10%."],"Points":["Prizes: see the Prizes section. In 2024 the champion received a total of PHP 125,000, which included the BingoPlus award."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The Festival Music Competition began in 2017. It is a sidelight of the Aliwan Fiesta competitions and highlights the musical talent of Filipinos from all over the country.\\n- It is held on the first day of the festival. In 2024 it was on June 27 at 5 PM in front of the Aliw Theater.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The presentation lasts at least four (4) minutes and at most five (5) minutes.\\n- A penalty of one (1) point is taken from the total score of all judges for every 10 seconds below four (4) minutes or beyond five (5) minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each ensemble must present a medley of one song endemic to the area or region it represents, mashed with one verse and one stanza of the Aliwan theme song.\\n- Open to all official musicians of the contingents that take part in the festival dance competition.\\n- Groups must perform in full costume.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Movements that unduly endanger the safety of the musicians are prohibited.\\n- No electronic instruments, pre-recorded instrumentation or vocals.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Musicality (arrangement, tonal quality, harmony): 50%. Showmanship (dynamics and technique, including costumes and choreography): 40%. Audience impact: 10%.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Prizes: see the Prizes section. In 2024 the champion received a total of PHP 125,000, which included the BingoPlus award."},{"Title":"Aliwan Fiesta Photography Competition","Source":"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (Is there a photo competition?); Update 'Aliwan Fiesta Photo Competition: Showcasing talents through photography' (18 Jun 2024); Update 'Aliwan Fiesta 2024 announces photography competition winners' (21 Aug 2024); Updates 'Meet the photo competition winners of Aliwan Fiesta 2023' (19 Sep 2023) and 'Indayog wins Aliwan Fiesta 2023 photo competition' (15 Nov 2023)","Sections":{"About":["The competition highlights Philippine culture and honours the talents of Filipino photographers. Photographers show their skills during the celebration of Aliwan Fiesta.","The FAQs say Aliwan Fiesta will mount a photo competition again this year, and to wait for further announcements."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Open to amateur and professional photographers (2024 announcement).","Winning entries become the property of MBC Media Group. The organiser can publish or exhibit the material for promotional purposes. The owner of the photo is still named when it is posted.","A panel of judges scores the entries. In 2024 it had three judges and in 2023 it had three judges.","In 2023 the awards were given at Fort Santiago in Intramuros, Manila, with the winners' photos shown at an exhibition. Winners who were not present could claim prizes at the MBC office in Pasay City."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Prizes: see the Prizes section. In 2023 the top three received PHP 50,000, 25,000 and 10,000 and the other seven of the top 10 received PHP 2,000 each.","In 2024 the first, second and third places were awarded as above. The announcement said PHP 2,500 for eight consolation winners; the results list seven consolation names, each receiving PHP 2,500."],"Notes":["The deadline for 2026 is not announced yet. In 2024 the deadline for submissions was July 12, 2024."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The competition highlights Philippine culture and honours the talents of Filipino photographers. Photographers show their skills during the celebration of Aliwan Fiesta.\\n- The FAQs say Aliwan Fiesta will mount a photo competition again this year, and to wait for further announcements.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Open to amateur and professional photographers (2024 announcement).\\n- Winning entries become the property of MBC Media Group. The organiser can publish or exhibit the material for promotional purposes. The owner of the photo is still named when it is posted.\\n- A panel of judges scores the entries. In 2024 it had three judges and in 2023 it had three judges.\\n- In 2023 the awards were given at Fort Santiago in Intramuros, Manila, with the winners' photos shown at an exhibition. Winners who were not present could claim prizes at the MBC office in Pasay City.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Prizes: see the Prizes section. In 2023 the top three received PHP 50,000, 25,000 and 10,000 and the other seven of the top 10 received PHP 2,000 each.\\n- In 2024 the first, second and third places were awarded as above. The announcement said PHP 2,500 for eight consolation winners; the results list seven consolation names, each receiving PHP 2,500.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The deadline for 2026 is not announced yet. In 2024 the deadline for submissions was July 12, 2024."},{"Title":"Reyna ng Aliwan","Source":"Aliwan Fiesta Activities pages (Reyna ng Aliwan); Update 'Festival Queen search reaches a fever pitch at Aliwan Fiesta 2024' (19 Jun 2024); Update 'Aliwan Fiesta 2024 unveils festivities with a press conference and official presentation of Reyna ng Aliwan Candidates' (24 Jun 2024); Update 'Aliwan Fiesta Highlights: Festival queens graced the Aliw Theater stage, honored with special awards' (29 Jun 2024); Update 'Dinagyang Festival Secures Back-to-Back Win, Pasigarbo Festival Reigns as Reyna ng Aliwan 2024' (30 Jun 2024); Update 'Aliwan Fiesta 2023 wraps up the Grand Parade with the best of the best' (15 Jul 2023); Update 'Rising from the ashes: The spectacular return of Aliwan Fiesta this 2023' (24 May 2023); Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026)","Sections":{"About":["Reyna ng Aliwan is the annual festival queen pageant. Candidates represent their respective festivals and cultures and show beauty and intellectual aptitude. It has been held since 2003 and is one of the three main highlights of Aliwan Fiesta."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Candidates are aged 16 and above and represent festivals of their hometowns.","Candidates must be naturally born women according to the competition mechanics (statement at the 2024 press conference).","Local government units (LGUs) may field entries for the search for Festival Queen (2023 announcement).","The program has a festival costume competition that ends in the Grand Parade, a swimsuit segment, and an evening gown presentation in which contestants answer questions from the judges.","The winner takes part in promotional activities for Aliwan Fiesta and other MBC Media Group events. She must not join any other beauty pageant until she gives her crown to her successor.","Netizens' Choice Award: the public can vote for a favourite candidate online. You can vote twice per day. You must register on the website to vote. The voting site is announced for 2026: {{NetizensVoteSite}} Last day of voting: {{NetizensVoteEnd}}"],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Personality: 35%. Beauty and poise: 35%. Costume: 20%. Overall impact: 10%. Total 100%. The same criteria are printed for audiences who watch on digital platforms."],"Points":["Awards printed for 2024 and 2023: Reyna ng Aliwan, first runner-up, three 2nd runners-up, Best in Festival Costume and the Netizens' Choice award.","Special awards printed for 2024: Miss Friendship, Miss Photogenic, Darling of the Press, Miss Unique Smile, Miss Charm, Miss White Rose, Best in Swimsuit, Best in Evening Gown. The Best in Festival Costume and Netizens' Choice awards were also given.","The prize money is in the Prizes section."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Reyna ng Aliwan is the annual festival queen pageant. Candidates represent their respective festivals and cultures and show beauty and intellectual aptitude. It has been held since 2003 and is one of the three main highlights of Aliwan Fiesta.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Candidates are aged 16 and above and represent festivals of their hometowns.\\n- Candidates must be naturally born women according to the competition mechanics (statement at the 2024 press conference).\\n- Local government units (LGUs) may field entries for the search for Festival Queen (2023 announcement).\\n- The program has a festival costume competition that ends in the Grand Parade, a swimsuit segment, and an evening gown presentation in which contestants answer questions from the judges.\\n- The winner takes part in promotional activities for Aliwan Fiesta and other MBC Media Group events. She must not join any other beauty pageant until she gives her crown to her successor.\\n- Netizens' Choice Award: the public can vote for a favourite candidate online. You can vote twice per day. You must register on the website to vote. The voting site is announced for 2026: {{NetizensVoteSite}} Last day of voting: {{NetizensVoteEnd}}\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Personality: 35%. Beauty and poise: 35%. Costume: 20%. Overall impact: 10%. Total 100%. The same criteria are printed for audiences who watch on digital platforms.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Awards printed for 2024 and 2023: Reyna ng Aliwan, first runner-up, three 2nd runners-up, Best in Festival Costume and the Netizens' Choice award.\\n- Special awards printed for 2024: Miss Friendship, Miss Photogenic, Darling of the Press, Miss Unique Smile, Miss Charm, Miss White Rose, Best in Swimsuit, Best in Evening Gown. The Best in Festival Costume and Netizens' Choice awards were also given.\\n- The prize money is in the Prizes section."}]`),s=[],r=[{Key:"EventStartDate",Kind:"date",Label:"First day of Aliwan Fiesta 2026",Value:"2026-05-07",Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (When is Aliwan Fiesta 2026? May 7-9, 2026)"},{Key:"EventEndDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Last day of Aliwan Fiesta 2026",Value:"2026-05-09",Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (When is Aliwan Fiesta 2026? May 7-9, 2026)"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Event venue",Value:{Name:"To be announced. The FAQs say: Kindly wait for announcements",Address:"",City:"",MapUrl:"",Directions:"The 2024 festival was held at the CCP Complex in Pasay City, with the Aliw Theater stage. The 2024 parade went along Jalandoni St. and V. Sotto St., P. Bukaneg St. in front of the CCP, Roxas Blvd., and ended in front of the Aliw Theater."},Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (Where does Aliwan Fiesta 2026 take place?) and Update 'Aliwan Fiesta, the festival of champions, is back!' (30 May 2024)"},{Key:"StartTime",Kind:"text",Label:"Start time of events",Value:"Kindly wait for announcements",Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (What time do events start?)"},{Key:"EntryDeadline",Kind:"text",Label:"Deadline for submission of entries",Value:"Kindly wait for announcements. (For 2023 the notice printed: Deadline for registration is on June 16.)",Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (When is the deadline for submission of entries?) and Update 'Streetdance & Float Competitions at Aliwan Fiesta 2023' (9 Jun 2023)"},{Key:"HowToRegister",Kind:"text",Label:"How participants register for competitions",Value:"Send inquiries to the Aliwan Secretariat. Kindly wait for announcements.",Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (How can participants register on competitions?)"},{Key:"RegistrationEmail2023",Kind:"contact",Label:"Contact printed in the 2023 registration notice",Value:{Name:"Aliwan Fiesta (2023 enquiries)",Role:"Enquiries about the 2023 streetdance and float registration",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"eloi@mbcradio.net"},Source:"Update 'Streetdance & Float Competitions at Aliwan Fiesta 2023' (9 Jun 2023)"},{Key:"BazaarContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Contact: Regional Bazaar slots",Value:{Name:"Ms. Teresa Rivas",Role:"Regional Bazaar booth inquiries",Phone:"8832-3249 / 0917-865-8699 / 0916-614-6102 / 0926-052-5744",WhatsApp:"",Email:"aliwanfiesta.bazaar@gmail.com (printed in the 2024 bazaar update)"},Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (How to secure a slot or register on the Regional Bazaar?) and Update 'The Aliwan Fiesta Shoppers' Bazaar: Elevating your cultural shopping experience' (15 May 2024)"},{Key:"BazaarEmail2023",Kind:"contact",Label:"Bazaar contacts printed in 2023",Value:{Name:"Teray Rivas / Leny Vicente / Davon Panzo",Role:"Shoppers Bazaar enquiries (2023)",Phone:"02.8832.3249 / 0917.865.8699 / 0917.866.3973 / 0956.634.2511",WhatsApp:"",Email:"aliwanfest.2023@gmail.com"},Source:"Update 'Opportunities for Regional Trade at Aliwan Fiesta' (7 Jun 2023)"},{Key:"StreetdanceGrandPrize",Kind:"text",Label:"Streetdance grand prize (last printed, 2023 and 2024)",Value:"PHP 1.5 million for the champion, with cash prizes for runners-up. In 2024 the champion also received PHP 25,000 from BingoPlus, and the Best in Costume award came with PHP 10,000.",Source:"Update 'Aliwan Fiesta 2024 reveals dance parade, float competition participants' (5 Jun 2024); Update 'Streetdance & Float Competitions at Aliwan Fiesta 2023' (9 Jun 2023); Update 'Iloilo festival leaders celebrate Dinagyang's historic Aliwan win' (9 Jul 2024)"},{Key:"FloatGrandPrize",Kind:"text",Label:"Float grand prize (last printed, 2023 and 2024)",Value:"PHP 750,000 for the grand winner, with cash prizes for runners-up.",Source:"Update 'Aliwan Fiesta 2024 reveals dance parade, float competition participants' (5 Jun 2024); Update 'Streetdance & Float Competitions at Aliwan Fiesta 2023' (9 Jun 2023)"},{Key:"ReynaPrize",Kind:"text",Label:"Reyna ng Aliwan prize (last printed, 2023)",Value:"PHP 150,000 for the Reyna ng Aliwan.",Source:"Update 'Streetdance & Float Competitions at Aliwan Fiesta 2023' (9 Jun 2023)"},{Key:"TugtogPrizes",Kind:"text",Label:"Tugtog ng Aliwan prizes (last printed, 2024)",Value:"Cash prizes to the top three contingents: first prize PHP 100,000, 2nd runner up PHP 50,000, 3rd runner up PHP 25,000.",Source:"Update 'Amplifying Filipino music heritage: Tugtog ng Aliwan is back!' (14 Jun 2024)"},{Key:"PhotoPrizes",Kind:"text",Label:"Photography competition prizes (last printed, 2024)",Value:"Winner PHP 50,000. Runners-up PHP 25,000 and PHP 10,000. PHP 2,500 to each of eight winners as consolation prizes for joining.",Source:"Update 'Aliwan Fiesta Photo Competition: Showcasing talents through photography' (18 Jun 2024)"},{Key:"PhotoDeadline",Kind:"text",Label:"Photography competition: last date to submit",Value:"Not announced for 2026. The FAQs say: Kindly wait for further announcements. (The 2024 deadline was July 12, 2024.)",Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (Is there a photo competition?) and Update 'Aliwan Fiesta Photo Competition: Showcasing talents through photography' (18 Jun 2024)"},{Key:"NetizensVoteLimit",Kind:"text",Label:"Netizens' Choice Awards: votes allowed",Value:"You can vote twice per day.",Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (How many times am I allowed to vote for the candidate on the Netizens' Choice Awards?)"},{Key:"NetizensVoteEnd",Kind:"text",Label:"Netizens' Choice Awards: last day of voting",Value:"Kindly wait for announcements",Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (When is the last day of voting for the Netizens' Choice Awards?)"},{Key:"NetizensVoteSite",Kind:"text",Label:"Reyna ng Aliwan Netizens' Choice voting site",Value:"The voting site will be open soon. (In 2024 voting was at www.aliwanfiesta.com.)",Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (How to vote for Reyna ng Aliwan Netizens' Choice Awards?) and Update 'Aliwan Fiesta unveils the Reyna ng Aliwan 2024 official list of candidates!' (24 Jun 2024)"},{Key:"Schedule2024",Kind:"text",Label:"Programme of the 2024 festival (for reference; 2026 programme not announced)",Value:"Day 1 (June 27, 2024): Tugtog ng Aliwan Competition at 5 p.m., Pasakalye Concert at 7 pm. Day 2 (June 28): Reyna ng Aliwan pageant. Day 3 (June 29): Grand Parade at 5 p.m. with the Streetdance and Float Competitions, and Awarding Ceremonies at 9 p.m.",Source:"Update 'Aliwan Fiesta, the festival of champions, is back!' (30 May 2024); Update 'Amplifying Filipino music heritage: Tugtog ng Aliwan is back!' (14 Jun 2024)"},{Key:"LiveCoverage",Kind:"text",Label:"Live coverage",Value:"Facebook Pages: Aliwan Fiesta, DZRH News, Love Radio Manila, Yes! FM Manila, Easy Rock Manila, Radyo Natin Nationwide, DZRH TV, including all the regional stations nationwide, or live on cable channel.",Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (Where can I watch the live coverage?)"},{Key:"SocialMedia",Kind:"text",Label:"Official social media",Value:"Facebook https://www.facebook.com/aliwanfiestaofficial ; X / Twitter https://x.com/aliwanfiesta ; Instagram https://www.instagram.com/aliwanfiesta ; TikTok https://www.tiktok.com/@aliwanfiesta ; YouTube https://www.youtube.com/@aliwanfiesta6252",Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026) (Where can I find information about events and schedule?) and site footer links"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"Notices printed on the FAQs page (2026)",Value:[{Date:"",Title:"Aliwan Fiesta 2026 dates",Text:"Aliwan Fiesta 2026 is set on May 7-9, 2026.",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/faqs"},{Date:"",Title:"Photo competition",Text:"Aliwan Fiesta will once again mount a photo competition this year. Kindly wait for further announcements.",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/faqs"},{Date:"",Title:"Traffic advisories and road closures",Text:"Traffic advisories will be published soon. This answers the questions about road closures and alternative routes during Aliwan Fiesta 2026.",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/faqs"},{Date:"",Title:"Netizens' Choice Awards voting",Text:"The voting site for the Reyna ng Aliwan Netizens' Choice Awards will be open soon.",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/faqs"},{Date:"",Title:"Registration of competition participants",Text:"Participants can send inquiries to the Aliwan Secretariat soon. Kindly wait for announcements.",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/faqs"}],Source:"Aliwan Fiesta FAQs page (2026)"}],l=[{Claim:"The rules, eligibility, criteria, prizes and award lists on this page are from the organiser's own website: the Activities pages, the 2026 FAQs page, and the organiser's published Updates of 2023 and 2024 (Streetdance & Float, Tugtog ng Aliwan, Photo Competition, Festival Queen search, the press conference, the results and the bazaar notices). Each row names its source.",SourceType:"Primary - the organiser's own website (Manila Broadcasting Company / MBC Media Group)",Source:"aliwanfiesta.com",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/faqs"},{Claim:"The site has no single rulebook. The 2026 edition has only the FAQs: dates May 7-9, 2026, and 'Kindly wait for announcements' for the venue, start times, entry deadline, registration, photo competition and voting dates. Facts taken from the 2023 or 2024 updates are marked with the year. Nothing was written from general knowledge.",SourceType:"Primary - the organiser's own website (Manila Broadcasting Company / MBC Media Group)",Source:"aliwanfiesta.com",Url:"https://aliwanfiesta.com/activities"}],d={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:t,Page:a,ParticipantTypes:n,AgeGroups:i,Competitions:o,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{i as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,o as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,a as Page,n as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,h as Year,d as default};
